{"content":[{"c":["HAZER-HATTICON"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Boundary marker along Israel’s northern perimeter (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.47.16","r":"Ezek.47.16","rawR":"Ezek.47.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.47.16","value":"Ezek.47.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 47:16"},"). In conjunction with the use of Hazar-enan in this context, and in comparison with ",{"href":"?bref=Num.34.9-10","r":"Num.34.9-10","rawR":"Num.34.9-10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.34.9-10","value":"Num.34.9-10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Numbers 34:9-10"},", it appears that Hazer-hatticon may represent a scribal error for Hazar-enan."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"HazerHatticon","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ez 47:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.47.16","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.47.16","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.47.16"},{"anchorText":"Numbers 34:9-10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.34.9-10","rawQueryValue":"Num.34.9-10","sourceRefExact":"Num.34.9-10"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2d93b22d9c9b8b9eb97409348b3c1be4be150a403afb3b838de2da5ed70d6ea0","sourceItemName":"HazerHatticon","sourceItemOrder":182,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"HazerHatticon","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hazer-Hatticon","title":"Hazer-Hatticon","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}